<title>POLAND: COMPUTERLAND TRADES ON KERB AT PLN 70.</title>
<headline>COMPUTERLAND TRADES ON KERB AT PLN 70.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Five kerb transactions in Polish software firm ComputerLand SA at 70 zlotys per share were struck on the Warsaw bourse on Monday, the bourse said in a statement.</p>
<p>The five trades were in blocks of 86,500, 25,000, 70,000, 30,000 and 40,000 shares.</p>
<p>At the regular bourse session ComputerLand traded at 71 zlotys in a volume of 18,825 shares.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
